meta-furilabs
=============

LuneOS machine support for FuriLabs phones.

Machines
--------

  radon    FuriPhone FLX1s - MediaTek Dimensity 900 (MT6877), 6.7" 720x1600,
           Linux 4.19.325.

This layer is unusual among the meta-smartphone layers in that the vendor
ships everything a port needs, in public, under their own name:

  github.com/furilabs/linux-furiphone-radon     the kernel tree (GPL, complete)
  github.com/furilabs/adaptation-furiphone-radon  the device adaptation package
  github.com/furilabs/radon-vendor-32           the Android 12L vendor image

FuriLabs' own distribution (FuriOS) is Debian-based and runs the same
libhybris + LXC Android container stack LuneOS does, so their kernel is
already configured for a glibc/systemd userspace. See radon.conf and
luneos.cfg for what that means in practice - the short version is that the
LuneOS kernel config delta for this device is very nearly empty, which is
true of no other port in this tree.

Two things this layer needs that are not in it:

  * Google's prebuilt Android Clang r416183b, which the kernel is built with -
    the release FuriLabs themselves pin, and the same one sunfish, q25, mp01
    and bramble already use. Point local.conf at it:

      GKI_CLANG_DIR:radon = ".../prebuilts-master/clang/host/linux-x86/clang-r416183b"

  * An install path. The FLX1s is flashed with MediaTek's SP Flash Tool (or
    mtkclient on Linux), NOT fastboot, so none of the fastboot install kits in
    this tree apply. Do not write preloader or super.

Port notes, fetch scripts and the config audit live in
~/webos/LuneOS/furilabs/radon.

Dependencies
